# Customer Segmentation Analysis using Python (K-Means) and Power BI
# Project Description
This project aims to analyze customer demographic and behavioral data to identify distinct customer segments using the K-Means clustering algorithm. The dataset was cleaned and preprocessed to handle missing values and ensure data quality. Important customer attributes such as Age, Gender, Profession, Work Experience, Family Size, and Spending Score were analyzed to discover meaningful patterns.

Python was used to perform customer segmentation using the K-Means clustering algorithm, while Power BI was used to create an interactive dashboard for visualizing customer segments, spending behavior, and demographic characteristics. The project helps businesses understand different customer groups, enabling more effective marketing strategies, personalized services, and improved customer retention.

# Project Objectives:-
- Clean and preprocess customer data by handling missing values and correcting data types.
- Analyze customer demographics such as age, gender, profession, marital status, and family size.
- Identify customer behavior using spending score and work experience.
- Apply the K-Means clustering algorithm to group customers with similar characteristics.
- Build an interactive Power BI dashboard to visualize customer segments and key performance indicators (KPIs).
- Generate business insights that support targeted marketing campaigns and customer relationship management.
- Improve decision-making by identifying high-value customer groups and understanding customer preferences.

# Expected Outcomes:-
- Identified meaningful customer segments using machine learning.
- Visualized customer characteristics through interactive Power BI dashboards.
- Analyzed demographic and behavioral patterns for better business understanding.
- Provided actionable insights for targeted marketing and customer engagement.
- Demonstrated practical skills in data cleaning, data analysis, machine learning, and business intelligence.

